+## Telegram interaction update — 2026-10-15
+
+Implemented for development acceptance; Lisa deployment and live dev checks
+remain pending. Repository contract and rollout: `docs/nexus-conversations.md`.
+
+- `/mode nexus` routes ordinary text to independent tasks; slash commands keep
+  their own handlers. Only the configured private `globalAdmin` can use Nexus,
+  with current-role checks on every operation.
+- Each task snapshots up to ten recent same-chat text messages (24 hours,
+  8,000 characters total); explicit quoted messages are included as reference.
+  History capture starts after deployment and never imports old Telegram chats.
+- Reply to a new Nexus completion explicitly resumes its provider session;
+  ordinary messages stay independent. Sessions are linear, not reply branches.
+  Missing sessions fail explicitly, without `--last` or an independent fallback.
+- Success messages contain the answer plus a separated model/token/time footer.
+  Token counts are compact; exact data stays in the audit/API. Accepted messages,
+  UUID headings and automatic retry messages are hidden.
+- Only `typing` status is used, refreshed from durable queue state and bounded
+  to 45 minutes per source record. No drafts or streaming.
+- Migration `6_nexus_conversations` adds interaction metadata, message mappings
+  and the short-lived history buffer. Workers advertise `supportsConversations`
+  when claiming; older workers cannot silently ignore new task context.
+- The local worker/shared dispatcher persist sessions only for interaction-bearing
+  tasks. Existing tasks and other automations keep their ephemeral behavior.
+  Session IDs stay in private local queue state and survive callback replay.
+
+The production LaunchAgent origin/credential and interval are unchanged. Use a
+separate dev origin/credential and queue directory for live acceptance; do not
+implicitly repoint the production poller. Automated verification uses fake AI
+executables and isolated PostgreSQL, without real AI or Telegram calls.
